      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(skills): load JSON5-style metadata frontmatter",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #108432.\n\nWorkspace skills can include OpenClaw metadata in `SKILL.md` frontmatter. The markdown-core skill metadata parser already tolerates JSON5-style flow mappings with trailing commas, but the session skill loader still used the generic agent frontmatter parser. That path throws on the same metadata block, so the skill is dropped even though the skill-specific parser can read it.\n\nThis patch makes the session skill loader use the skill frontmatter parser and the existing skill invocation policy helper. That keeps JSON5-style metadata loading aligned with the rest of skill metadata handling, while preserving `disable-model-invocation: true` behavior after the parser change.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact-head proof for `51ee064447a08f9589c687004272f093d73ca634`:\n\n- `PATH=\"...\" ./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/skills/loading/session.ts src/skills/loading/session.test.ts scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs src/infra/file-read.ts` -> passed\n- `PATH=\"...\" ./node_modules/.bin/oxlint src/skills/loading/session.ts src/skills/loading/session.test.ts` -> passed\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` -> passed\n- `PATH=\"...\" node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo` -> passed\n- `PATH=\"...\" node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/skills/loading/session.test.ts src/skills/loading/frontmatter.test.ts packages/markdown-core/src/frontmatter.test.ts test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts` -> passed; 3 Vitest shards, including the plugin SDK surface exact-budget test\n\nThe new focused test creates a `SKILL.md` with JSON5-style trailing commas in `metadata.openclaw.requires.env`, verifies `loadSkillsFromDir()` loads it with no diagnostics, verifies `disable-model-invocation: true` still works, and verifies the metadata env requirement parses as `EXAMPLE_VAR`.\n\nThe PR also updates the plugin SDK public surface budget from `10606` to `10605` because this change removes the session-only exported `SkillFrontmatter` interface from the public source graph.\n",
        "branch": "fix/108432-skill-frontmatter-json5",
